                            DEFINITIONS
================================================================================

"Software" means the Surge traffic generator application, including all 
associated binary files, documentation, configuration files, and any related 
materials provided by the Licensor.

"Licensor" means Harry-Not-Potter, the copyright holder and owner of the 
Software.

"Licensee" means any individual or entity that downloads, installs, or uses 
the Software.

"Binary Form" means the compiled, executable version of the Software as 
distributed in .deb packages or other executable formats.

"Source Code" means the human-readable source code of the Software, including 
but not limited to C++ source files, header files, build scripts, and 
configuration files used to compile the Software.

"Attribution" means a clear and visible statement that the Software was 
created by the Licensor, including the Licensor's name and a link to the 
project website, placed in:
    a) Any documentation, screenshots, or videos featuring the Software
    b) Any public presentations or demonstrations of the Software
    c) Any redistribution packages or repositories
    d) Any derivative configurations or scripts that use the Software

"Reverse Engineering" means any activity aimed at discovering the Source Code, 
underlying ideas, algorithms, or structure of the Software, including but not 
limited to:
    a) Disassembly, decompilation, or decryption of the Binary Form
    b) Analysis of network protocols, file formats, or data structures
    c) Debugging, tracing, or monitoring the Software's execution
    d) Memory dumping or runtime code analysis
    e) Using debuggers, tracers, or packet analyzers on the Software
    f) Any other method of deriving Source Code from Binary Form

"Permitted Use" means using the Software in Binary Form for its intended 
purpose as a traffic generation tool, subject to the Attribution requirement.

